From 25d15d1abf6d9ebf6382e5a7800c58d317c27fff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joey <joey@Mac-Studio.local>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:30:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mainloop: index connection_array, active_linked, and
 closeable cleanup scans

Replace linear O(N), O(A), and O(C) smartlist_contains/smartlist_remove scans across connection_array, active_linked_connection_lst, and closeable_connection_lst during connection teardown and linked-connection read activation/deactivation with O(1) index-tracked operations:

1. Introduce connection_in_idx_list(), CONN_IDX_LIST_ADD(), and CONN_IDX_LIST_DEL() to validate index bounds/pointer identity and perform swap-delete index repair in O(1) across connection_array, closeable_connection_lst, and active_linked_connection_lst.
2. Reset conn->conn_array_index to -1 in connection_remove().
3. Add conn->active_linked_conn_idx and conn->closeable_conn_idx (initialized to -1 in connection_init()) and maintain them in O(1) across add_connection_to_closeable_list(), connection_start_reading_from_linked_conn(), connection_stop_reading_from_linked_conn(), and connection_unlink().
4. Assert !connection_is_on_closeable_list(conn), !connection_in_array(conn), and !connection_in_active_linked_list(conn) in O(1) inside connection_free_().
5. Fix direct smartlist_add(get_connection_array(), ...) test helpers in test_conflux_pool.c and test_hs_client.c to maintain conn_array_index and remove connections before connection_free_minimal().
6. Add unit, peer-teardown, re-entrant mark-for-close, OOM-reindexing, corruption-assertion, and randomized lifecycle tests in test_mainloop.c.
